NAME
       visudo - edit the sudoers file safely

SYNOPSIS
       **visudo** [-chqsV] [[-f] __file__]

DESCRIPTION
       **visudo** must be run as root. It copies /etc/sudoers to
       /etc/sudoers.tmp (created exclusively, so two editors cannot run at
       once), starts $SUDO_EDITOR, $VISUAL, $EDITOR or vim, and parses the
       result with the same parser sudo uses. On success the file gets
       owner root, mode 0440 and replaces /etc/sudoers atomically. On a
       syntax error visudo prints "file:line: syntax error" and asks
       "What now?": (e) edit again, (x) exit without saving, (Q) quit and
       save anyway.

OPTIONS
       -c   check only: parse the file and all included files and print
            "parsed OK" for each.
       -f __file__  use __file__ instead of /etc/sudoers.
       -s   strict: unknown Defaults entries are errors.
       -q   quiet check.
       -h, -V  help, version.

SEE ALSO
       sudoers(5), sudo(8)
